# RISC Box "xorg" guest image — Buildroot defconfig (tested on 2024.02.x LTS).
#
# Produces the two files a RISC Box deployment boots:
#   images/fw_payload.elf  OpenSBI v0.9 with the Linux 5.15 Image as payload
#                          (built by guest/build-opensbi.sh AFTER this — see
#                          the OpenSBI note at the bottom)
#   images/rootfs.ext2     ext2 root with Xorg (fbdev) + twm + dropbear +
#                          the spincube demo (guest/cube.c)
#
# Version pins are deliberate, not stale: the vendored emulator is RV64GC,
# one hart, Sv39. Linux 5.15 is the last LTS that only ever uses Sv39 (5.17+
# probes Sv48 via satp round-trips) and predates any ISA-extension
# expectations beyond GC; OpenSBI 1.2 boots fine on CLINT+PLIC-era hardware
# models. Bump either only with a boot test on the emulator.
#
# Build (out of tree):
#   make O=$BUILD BR2_DEFCONFIG=$APP/guest/buildroot.config defconfig
#   RISCBOX_GUEST=$APP/guest make O=$BUILD -j$(nproc)
# guest/build.sh wraps exactly this.
BR2_riscv=y
# External prebuilt cross-toolchain (Bootlin, glibc). Building an internal
# gcc host-side fails on bleeding-edge host compilers (GCC 16 can't compile
# GCC 12's libcody); a downloaded toolchain sidesteps it — host gcc then only
# builds small host utilities (m4/autoconf/…), and the TARGET is built by the
# Bootlin gcc, not the host. Also much faster (no 3-stage gcc bootstrap).
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN_RISCV64_LP64D_GLIBC_STABLE=y
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_HOSTNAME="riscbox"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ISSUE="RISC Box xorg guest"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ROOT_PASSWD="riscbox"
BR2_SYSTEM_BIN_SH_BUSYBOX=y
# risc-box patch: eudev for device management. The kernel's devtmpfs already
# creates /dev/input/event0 for the virtio-input HID, but X's input drivers
# (libinput/evdev) hard-require libudev at BUILD time — Buildroot gates them on
# BR2_PACKAGE_HAS_UDEV, which only eudev/systemd provide. eudev supplies
# libudev (so libinput builds) and enumerates the device; X still binds it
# statically (xorg.conf, AutoAddDevices off) so input works deterministically
# regardless of hotplug timing.
BR2_ROOTFS_DEVICE_CREATION_DYNAMIC_EUDEV=y
# static 10.0.2.15 via the overlay's /etc/network/interfaces (the app's
# user-mode LAN answers DHCP too, but static boots faster and never races)
BR2_SYSTEM_DHCP=""
# Package patches (guest/patches/<pkg>/*.patch). The one patch that matters:
# xserver ddxLoad.c installs the overlay's prebuilt keymap instead of forking
# xkbcomp — the emulator can't survive Xorg's fork-of-xkbcomp (the child dies
# before exec) and keyboard init would abort. See the patch header.
BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR="$(RISCBOX_GUEST)/patches"
BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY="$(RISCBOX_GUEST)/overlay"
BR2_ROOTFS_POST_BUILD_SCRIPT="$(RISCBOX_GUEST)/post-build.sh"
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION_VALUE="5.15.164"
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_USE_ARCH_DEFAULT_CONFIG=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES="$(RISCBOX_GUEST)/kernel.fragment"
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_IMAGE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_DROPBEAR=y
# Xorg on /dev/fb0: the modular server + the fbdev driver, a window manager,
# and the libs cube.c needs. No GL anywhere — the guest renders in software.
BR2_PACKAGE_XORG7=y
BR2_PACKAGE_XSERVER_XORG_SERVER=y
BR2_PACKAGE_XSERVER_XORG_SERVER_MODULAR=y
BR2_PACKAGE_XDRIVER_XF86_VIDEO_FBDEV=y
# risc-box patch: the X input driver for the emulator's virtio-input HID.
# xf86-input-libinput (pulling libinput + libevdev + mtdev) reads the evdev
# node the guest kernel binds to virtio-input and hands X a pointer +
# keyboard — the interface a remote/streaming client's input arrives through.
BR2_PACKAGE_XDRIVER_XF86_INPUT_LIBINPUT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_XAPP_TWM=y
BR2_PACKAGE_XAPP_XSETROOT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_XLIB_LIBX11=y
# ext2, NOT ext4: the vendored emulator's virtio-blk completes reads of the
# ext2 sample fine, but an ext4 journal-inode read during mount hangs waiting
# for a completion that never arrives (no host panic — the guest just blocks).
# ext2 has no journal, so that path never runs. Keep the image modest (the
# known-good sample is a 50 MiB ext2); content here is ~40 MiB.
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2=y
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_2=y
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_SIZE="96M"
# fw_payload.elf: OpenSBI with the kernel Image embedded — the one-file boot
# artifact the emulator's ELF loader expects. Deliberately NOT built here:
# Buildroot 2024.02 carries OpenSBI 1.2, which builds position-independent
# (FW_PIC=y) firmware the emulator's ELF loader cannot relocate — the machine
# never reaches the SBI banner. guest/build-opensbi.sh builds v0.9 non-PIC
# with this config's own cross-toolchain right after make finishes;
# guest/build.sh runs both steps.
